  "id": "field-survey",
  "term": "field survey",
  "definition": "A field survey is a survey study carried out in a real-life setting rather than an artificial one, used to examine how experiences and psychological or social factors are related over time in a specific population. In this source, it refers to a three-wave, self-report design with repeated measurements to test prospective associations.",
